<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Firhun ag Alinsar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1916</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Firhun ag Alinsar was amenokal, paramount chief, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iwellemmeden">Iwellemmeden</a> Kel Ataram <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>. Made to submit to the French, he was imprisoned, escaped and in 1916, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, led a revolt against French rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> region. He was defeated and killed in 1916, and the confederation's power was broken.</p></div>
